{"ts":"2026-08-02T00:40:15.547Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"7d49453d0d45fcc94817af12","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-y3w0ld"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-864: history-redact output must never echo literal secrets"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue #864 demonstrates that the audited redaction mutation rewrites history safely but returns the original literal matcher under patterns.literals, copying the value into terminal logs, CI output, agent transcripts, and SDK/MCP responses. Make the result contract disclosure-safe across applied, dry-run, no-op, and failure paths while preserving deterministic matcher counts and auditability."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","area:security","history","privacy","redaction"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-02T00:40:15.547Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-02T00:40:15.547Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Raw literal matcher values are absent from TOON, JSON, SDK, MCP, dry-run, no-op, error, telemetry, and profile outputs; regex matcher source receives equally safe treatment because pattern text may itself be sensitive; results retain deterministic matcher-kind counts and replacement/change counts without reversible matcher material; regression tests use canary matchers and assert absence from serialized success, dry-run, no-op, and failure surfaces; public SDK types and operator documentation define the disclosure-safe result contract; full 100/100/100/100 coverage, security scan, contract gates, and isolated temporary-directory acceptance pass"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"A secret supplied for audited removal is never repeated by the command that removes it"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"History redaction must reduce disclosure, never multiply it into output and observability surfaces"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Changes the public HistoryRedactResult pattern summary to non-reversible metadata and hardens CLI, SDK, MCP, telemetry, and tests against canary disclosure"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Applied, preview, no-op, and rejected redaction invocations expose useful counts without returning matcher content"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-4a7m"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"74f74af61783bfa537b24d35f7bb25305b0b0f25f0a7d43ac5371dcabff3e5eb","message":"Duplicate check: all-status keyword searches for history-redact and redaction secrets found canonical delivered command pm-xk39, SDK owner pm-4a7m, and broader write-time guard gap pm-wwooxx, but no item for output echoing supplied matcher content. Creating the narrow security regression item and linking it to those existing lineages plus GH-864."}
